   <p>So I don't treat this as cleanup work. Tracing a definition back to where it forked is the point where the business's language and the warehouse's tables finally have to agree, and that's the most useful modeling work available. The finding is rarely that one report is broken. It's that a decision was made years ago, never written down, and is now nobody's.</p>
   <p class="review-line">Reviewed 24 November 2026. The tracing method here is not tied to a tool version, but the ways definitions drift do change with how teams build. If your versions of this story end differently, <a href="mailto:tulashobhan@gmail.com">tell me</a>.</p>
